# Admin panel (Vite) environment template.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust values for your machine. Only variables
# prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser bundle — never put secrets here.
#
# The panel reads this value in src/lib/api/config.ts (import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL)
# and falls back to http://localhost:4000/api/v1 when it is not set.

# Base URL of the backend API the panel talks to. Must include the /api/v1 mount
# point. The backend CORS policy allows the dev origins below.
#
# Local development (backend on http://localhost:4000, panel on http://localhost:5173):
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api/v1
#
# LAN / device testing (backend reachable at a machine IP):
# VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:4000/api/v1
#
# Production (same-origin reverse proxy in front of the API):
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api/v1
